**Gates before launch**

I will not launch the round until four gates pass, in this order. First, I confirm that spe/predictions/r04.yaml and spe/plans/r04.md are committed and have not changed since that commit. Second, I run the grader selftest with `python3 spe/evals/graders/grade.py --selftest`. The oracle answers must pass on all 50 tickets. An empty output must fail, and so must an output with wrong labels. I also run judge.md on two replies I know are good and two I know are bad, to check that it tells them apart. Third, I regrade round 3's saved outputs with this round's grade.py as a control. Those numbers must match round 3's recorded numbers. If they move, the grader changed, and I log that in spe/failures.md before I launch. Fourth, I save this script as spe/evals/harness/r04-workflow.js and commit it. Then I run a dry run with `only: ['B:T001', 'C2:T002'], trials: 1, topupMax: 0, budgetUsd: 2`. The dry run writes to spe/runs/r04-dry, so its outputs never mix with the real run. I check that each dry trial returns labels, a grade row, a judge score, and a cost. Only after that do I launch the full run with `gates: {selftest: 'pass', control: 'pass', dryRun: 'pass'}`. I made two assumptions. The triage CLI is `node triage/cli.js`, and the tickets are in spe/evals/tasks/tickets/<id>.json. My spend estimates of $0.04 per trial and $0.02 per judged reply are guesses I have not measured.

**spe/evals/harness/r04-workflow.js**

```js
export const meta = {
  name: 'triage-spe-eval',
  description: 'SPE eval for the triage agent. Configs B and C2, fixed tickets and graders, code grader first, Opus tone judge second, spend cap from args.',
  phases: [
    { title: 'Preflight' },
    { title: 'Trials' },
    { title: 'Leak scan' },
    { title: 'Grade' },
    { title: 'Judge' },
    { title: 'Top-up' },
    { title: 'Synthesis' },
  ],
};

// ---------- Round and arguments ----------
const A = typeof args === 'undefined' || args == null ? {} : args;
const ROUND = A.round ?? 4;
const RR = String(ROUND).padStart(2, '0');
const DRY = Array.isArray(A.only) && A.only.length > 0;
const CONFIGS = A.configs ?? ['B', 'C2'];          // CLI presets: B = 12-line prompt, 6 tools. C2 = 12-line prompt, 3 tools + check_status.
const TICKETS = A.tickets;                          // ticket IDs only, never labels
const EXPECTED_TICKETS = A.expectedTickets ?? 50;
const TRIALS = A.trials ?? 5;
const TOPUP_MAX = A.topupMax ?? 5;                  // extra trials per split cell
const BUDGET_USD = A.budgetUsd ?? 40;               // cap on triage API spend plus judge spend
const EST_TRIAL_USD = A.estTrialUsd ?? 0.04;        // unmeasured estimate, used for reservations
const EST_JUDGE_USD = A.estJudgeUsd ?? 0.02;        // unmeasured estimate per judged reply
const MAX_AGENTS = A.maxAgents ?? 320;              // cap on Workflow agents (wrappers, graders, judges)
const MAX_VOID_FRACTION = A.maxVoidFraction ?? 0.05;
const TRIAGE_MODEL = A.triageModel ?? 'claude-sonnet-5-5';
const HARNESS_MODEL = A.harnessModel ?? 'opus';
const JUDGE_MODEL = A.judgeModel ?? 'opus';
const RUN_DIR = `spe/runs/r${RR}${DRY ? '-dry' : ''}`;
const FORBIDDEN = [
  'spe/evals/graders', 'spe/evals/tasks/answers.json', 'answers.json',
  'spe/predictions', 'spe/plans', 'spe/prediction-log.md', 'judge.md',
];

// ---------- Input checks ----------
if (!Array.isArray(TICKETS) || TICKETS.length === 0) throw new Error('args.tickets must list ticket IDs');
if (!DRY && TICKETS.length !== EXPECTED_TICKETS) {
  throw new Error(`expected ${EXPECTED_TICKETS} tickets, got ${TICKETS.length}`);
}
if (!DRY) {
  const g = A.gates ?? {};
  for (const k of ['selftest', 'control', 'dryRun']) {
    if (g[k] !== 'pass') throw new Error(`gate ${k} has not passed. Run the gates before the full launch.`);
  }
}

// ---------- Schemas ----------
const PRE_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['prediction_committed', 'inputs_unchanged', 'selftest_pass', 'run_dir_empty', 'notes'],
  properties: {
    prediction_committed: { type: 'boolean' },
    inputs_unchanged: { type: 'boolean' },
    selftest_pass: { type: 'boolean' },
    run_dir_empty: { type: 'boolean' },
    notes: { type: 'string' },
  },
};

const TRIAL_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['config', 'ticket', 'trials', 'commands_run'],
  properties: {
    config: { type: 'string' },
    ticket: { type: 'string' },
    commands_run: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
    trials: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        required: ['trial', 'status', 'out_path', 'trace_path', 'cost_usd'],
        properties: {
          trial: { type: 'integer' },
          status: { enum: ['completed', 'harness_error', 'rate_limited'] },
          out_path: { type: 'string' },
          trace_path: { type: 'string' },
          category: { type: 'string' },
          priority: { type: 'string' },
          reply: { type: 'string' },
          runtime_s: { type: 'number' },
          tool_calls: { type: 'integer' },
          tool_errors: { type: 'integer' },
          input_tokens: { type: 'integer' },
          output_tokens: { type: 'integer' },
          cost_usd: { type: 'number' },
          error: { type: 'string' },
        },
      },
    },
  },
};

const LEAK_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['flagged_traces'],
  properties: { flagged_traces: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } } },
};

const GRADE_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['rows'],
  properties: {
    grader_error: { type: 'string' },
    rows: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        required: ['ticket', 'trial', 'category_ok', 'priority_ok'],
        properties: {
          ticket: { type: 'string' },
          trial: { type: 'integer' },
          category_ok: { type: 'boolean' },
          priority_ok: { type: 'boolean' },
        },
      },
    },
  },
};

const JUDGE_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['scores'],
  properties: {
    scores: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        required: ['id', 'tone_score', 'tone_pass', 'reason'],
        properties: {
          id: { type: 'string' },
          tone_score: { type: 'integer', minimum: 1, maximum: 5 },
          tone_pass: { type: 'boolean' },
          reason: { type: 'string' },
        },
      },
    },
  },
};

const FAILURE_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['failure_types', 'suspected_grader_bugs', 'proposals_next_round'],
  properties: {
    failure_types: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        required: ['name', 'kind', 'what', 'how_to_spot', 'seen_in', 'suggested_fix'],
        properties: {
          name: { type: 'string' },
          kind: { enum: ['agent', 'grader', 'judge', 'harness', 'task'] },
          what: { type: 'string' },
          how_to_spot: { type: 'string' },
          seen_in: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
          suggested_fix: { type: 'string' },
        },
      },
    },
    suspected_grader_bugs: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
    proposals_next_round: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
  },
};

const CRITIC_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['complete', 'gaps', 'unmeasured_predictions'],
  properties: {
    complete: { type: 'boolean' },
    gaps: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
    unmeasured_predictions: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
  },
};

// ---------- Budget and agent caps ----------
let spent = 0;
let reserved = 0;
let overrun = false;
let agentsUsed = 0;
const skips = [];

function reserve(usd) {
  if (overrun || spent + reserved + usd > BUDGET_USD) return false;
  reserved += usd;
  return true;
}
function settle(reservedUsd, actualUsd) {
  reserved -= reservedUsd;
  spent += actualUsd;
  if (spent > BUDGET_USD) {
    overrun = true;
    log(`Spend ${spent.toFixed(2)} passed the cap ${BUDGET_USD}. No new paid work will start.`);
  }
}
async function run(prompt, opts) {
  if (agentsUsed >= MAX_AGENTS) throw new Error(`agent cap ${MAX_AGENTS} reached`);
  agentsUsed += 1;
  return agent(prompt, { model: HARNESS_MODEL, ...opts });
}

// ---------- Helpers ----------
const range = (a, b) => Array.from({ length: Math.max(0, b - a + 1) }, (_, i) => a + i);
const mean = (xs) => (xs.length ? xs.reduce((s, x) => s + x, 0) / xs.length : null);
const tkey = (t) => `${t.config}:${t.ticket}:${t.trial}`;
function blindId(t) {
  let h = 5381;
  const s = `${ROUND}|${t.config}|${t.ticket}|${t.trial}`;
  for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) h = ((h * 33) ^ s.charCodeAt(i)) >>> 0;
  return `r${h.toString(36)}`;
}

const onlySet = DRY ? new Set(A.only) : null;
const cells = [];
for (const config of CONFIGS) {
  for (const ticket of TICKETS) {
    const key = `${config}:${ticket}`;
    if (!onlySet || onlySet.has(key)) cells.push({ config, ticket, key });
  }
}
if (cells.length === 0) throw new Error('no cells selected. Check args.only against config and ticket IDs.');

const trials = new Map(); // tkey -> record

// ---------- Prompts ----------
function trialPrompt(cell, nums, dir) {
  return `You are a harness runner. You run the triage agent CLI and report what it wrote. Do not judge, fix, or rerun output that looks wrong.

Run this command once for each trial number N in [${nums.join(', ')}], one at a time, from the repo root:
  node triage/cli.js --config ${cell.config} --model ${TRIAGE_MODEL} --ticket-id ${cell.ticket} --out ${dir}/t<N>.json --trace ${dir}/t<N>.trace.jsonl

After each run, read only that trial's --out file. It holds label.category, label.priority, reply, and a usage block with runtime_s, tool_calls, tool_errors, input_tokens, output_tokens, and cost_usd. Copy those values into the result.

You may read only files under ${dir}/. Do not open, list, grep, or cat anything under spe/evals/, spe/predictions/, spe/plans/, or spe/prediction-log.md.

If the CLI exits non-zero, set status to harness_error and put its last 5 output lines in error. If it reports a rate limit, wait 30 seconds and retry once. If it fails again, set status to rate_limited. Then move on to the next trial.

List every shell command you ran in commands_run, exactly as you ran it.`;
}

// ---------- Stages ----------
async function runCell(cell, nums, phaseName) {
  const granted = [];
  for (const n of nums) {
    if (reserve(EST_TRIAL_USD)) granted.push(n);
    else skips.push({ kind: 'trial', key: `${cell.key}:${n}`, reason: 'spend cap' });
  }
  if (granted.length === 0) return [];
  const dir = `${RUN_DIR}/${cell.config}/${cell.ticket}`;
  let res;
  try {
    res = await run(trialPrompt(cell, granted, dir), {
      label: `trial ${cell.key} t${granted.join(',')}`,
      phase: phaseName,
      schema: TRIAL_SCHEMA,
    });
  } catch (e) {
    settle(granted.length * EST_TRIAL_USD, 0);
    return granted.map((n) => ({ ...cell, trial: n, status: 'harness_error', error: String(e) }));
  }
  const reported = new Map((res.trials ?? []).map((t) => [t.trial, t]));
  const actual = [...reported.values()].reduce((s, t) => s + (t.cost_usd ?? 0), 0);
  settle(granted.length * EST_TRIAL_USD, actual);
  const peeked = (res.commands_run ?? []).some((c) => FORBIDDEN.some((p) => c.includes(p)));
  return granted.map((n) => {
    const t = reported.get(n) ?? { trial: n, status: 'harness_error', error: 'runner returned no record' };
    return {
      ...cell, ...t, trial: n,
      voided: peeked,
      void_reason: peeked ? 'runner command touched a forbidden path' : null,
    };
  });
}

async function leakScan(phaseName) {
  const pattern = FORBIDDEN.map((p) => p.replace(/\./g, '\\.')).join('|');
  const r = await run(`Run this one command from the repo root. Report every path it prints, exactly as printed. Do not open any other file.
grep -rlE '${pattern}' ${RUN_DIR} --include='*.trace.jsonl' || true`, {
    label: 'leak scan', phase: phaseName, schema: LEAK_SCHEMA,
  });
  const flagged = new Set(r.flagged_traces ?? []);
  for (const t of trials.values()) {
    if (t.trace_path && flagged.has(t.trace_path) && !t.voided) {
      t.voided = true;
      t.void_reason = 'trace shows a read of a grader, answer key, or prediction path';
    }
  }
  return flagged.size;
}

async function grade(phaseName) {
  const results = await parallel(CONFIGS.map((config) => () => run(
    `You run the code grader and report its output unchanged. Do not edit grade.py, answers.json, or any run file.
Run from the repo root:
  python3 spe/evals/graders/grade.py --answers spe/evals/tasks/answers.json --runs ${RUN_DIR}/${config} --json
The grader checks label.category and label.priority in each t<N>.json against answers.json. Copy each row it prints into rows. If the command exits non-zero or prints no rows, set grader_error to its last 20 lines and return no rows.`,
    { label: `grade ${config}`, phase: phaseName, schema: GRADE_SCHEMA },
  ).then((r) => ({ config, r }))));
  const errors = [];
  for (const { config, r } of results) {
    if (r.grader_error) errors.push(`${config}: ${r.grader_error}`);
    for (const row of r.rows ?? []) {
      const t = trials.get(`${config}:${row.ticket}:${row.trial}`);
      if (!t) continue;
      t.graded = true;
      t.category_ok = row.category_ok;
      t.priority_ok = row.priority_ok;
      t.both_ok = row.category_ok && row.priority_ok;
    }
  }
  return errors;
}

async function judge(records, phaseName) {
  const byTicket = new Map();
  for (const t of records) {
    if (t.status !== 'completed' || t.voided || !t.reply) continue;
    if (!byTicket.has(t.ticket)) byTicket.set(t.ticket, []);
    byTicket.get(t.ticket).push(t);
  }
  await parallel([...byTicket.entries()].map(([ticket, items]) => async () => {
    const granted = items.filter((t) => {
      if (reserve(EST_JUDGE_USD)) return true;
      skips.push({ kind: 'judge', key: tkey(t), reason: 'spend cap' });
      return false;
    });
    if (granted.length === 0) return;
    const idMap = new Map(granted.map((t) => [blindId(t), t]));
    const blind = [...idMap.entries()]
      .sort((a, b) => a[0].localeCompare(b[0]))
      .map(([id, t]) => ({ id, reply: t.reply }));
    try {
      const r = await run(`You are a tone judge. Read spe/evals/graders/judge.md and score each reply exactly as it says. Read the ticket from spe/evals/tasks/tickets/${ticket}.json. Do not read answers.json or anything under spe/predictions/. You do not know which configuration wrote which reply. Score each reply on its own, not against the others.

Replies:
${JSON.stringify(blind, null, 2)}`, {
        label: `judge ${ticket}`, phase: phaseName, schema: JUDGE_SCHEMA, model: JUDGE_MODEL,
      });
      for (const s of r.scores ?? []) {
        const t = idMap.get(s.id);
        if (!t) continue;
        t.tone_score = s.tone_score;
        t.tone_pass = s.tone_pass;
        t.tone_reason = s.reason;
      }
    } finally {
      settle(granted.length * EST_JUDGE_USD, granted.length * EST_JUDGE_USD); // judge spend is estimated, not measured
    }
  }));
}

function voidCheck() {
  const all = [...trials.values()];
  const voided = all.filter((t) => t.voided).length;
  return { voided, total: all.length, fraction: all.length ? voided / all.length : 0 };
}

function halt(reason) {
  log(`HALT: ${reason}`);
  return { round: ROUND, halted: true, reason, spent_usd: spent, agents_used: agentsUsed, skips, void: voidCheck() };
}

// ---------- Preflight ----------
phase('Preflight');
const pre = await run(`You check that the eval inputs are frozen before trials start. Run these commands from the repo root and report the results. Do not edit any file.
1. git ls-files --error-unmatch spe/predictions/r${RR}.yaml
2. git diff --quiet HEAD -- spe/predictions/r${RR}.yaml spe/evals/graders spe/evals/tasks/answers.json; echo exit=$?
3. python3 spe/evals/graders/grade.py --selftest
4. ls -A ${RUN_DIR} 2>/dev/null | head -5
Set prediction_committed to true only if command 1 succeeds. Set inputs_unchanged to true only if command 2 prints exit=0. Set selftest_pass to true only if command 3 exits 0 and reports that the oracle passes and that the empty and wrong answers fail. Set run_dir_empty to true if command 4 prints nothing.`, {
  label: 'preflight', phase: 'Preflight', schema: PRE_SCHEMA,
});
if (!pre.prediction_committed) return halt(`spe/predictions/r${RR}.yaml is not committed`);
if (!pre.inputs_unchanged) return halt('prediction, graders, or answer key changed since the last commit');
if (!pre.selftest_pass) return halt(`grader selftest failed: ${pre.notes}`);
if (!pre.run_dir_empty) return halt(`${RUN_DIR} already holds output. Move it before rerunning.`);
log(`Round ${ROUND}${DRY ? ' dry run' : ''}: ${cells.length} cells, ${TRIALS} trials each, cap $${BUDGET_USD}, run dir ${RUN_DIR}`);

// ---------- Trials ----------
phase('Trials');
const firstPass = (await parallel(cells.map((c) => () => runCell(c, range(1, TRIALS), 'Trials')))).flat();
for (const t of firstPass) trials.set(tkey(t), t);
log(`Trials: ${firstPass.length} run, ${firstPass.filter((t) => t.status === 'completed').length} completed, ${skips.length} skipped for the cap, spent $${spent.toFixed(2)}`);

// ---------- Leak scan ----------
phase('Leak scan');
await leakScan('Leak scan');
let vc = voidCheck();
log(`Leak scan: ${vc.voided} of ${vc.total} trials voided`);
if (vc.fraction > MAX_VOID_FRACTION) return halt(`${vc.voided} of ${vc.total} trials read forbidden paths. The answer key may be exposed.`);

// ---------- Grade ----------
phase('Grade');
let gradeErrors = await grade('Grade');
if (gradeErrors.length) return halt(`grader error: ${gradeErrors.join(' | ')}`);

// ---------- Judge ----------
phase('Judge');
await judge(firstPass, 'Judge');

// ---------- Top-up ----------
phase('Top-up');
const splitCells = cells.filter((c) => {
  const ts = [...trials.values()].filter((t) =>
    `${t.config}:${t.ticket}` === c.key && t.trial <= TRIALS && t.status === 'completed' && !t.voided && t.graded);
  const passes = ts.filter((t) => t.both_ok).length;
  return passes > 0 && passes < ts.length;
});
log(`Top-up: ${splitCells.length} split cells, up to ${TOPUP_MAX} extra trials each`);
if (TOPUP_MAX > 0 && splitCells.length > 0) {
  const extra = (await parallel(splitCells.map((c) =>
    () => runCell(c, range(TRIALS + 1, TRIALS + TOPUP_MAX), 'Top-up')))).flat();
  for (const t of extra) trials.set(tkey(t), t);
  await leakScan('Top-up');
  vc = voidCheck();
  if (vc.fraction > MAX_VOID_FRACTION) return halt(`${vc.voided} of ${vc.total} trials read forbidden paths after top-up`);
  gradeErrors = await grade('Top-up');
  if (gradeErrors.length) return halt(`grader error after top-up: ${gradeErrors.join(' | ')}`);
  await judge(extra, 'Top-up');
}

// ---------- Metrics ----------
// Headline metrics use only the planned trials (1..TRIALS) so that top-up does not weight split cells.
function summarize(config, planned) {
  const ts = [...trials.values()].filter((t) => t.config === config && (planned ? t.trial <= TRIALS : t.trial > TRIALS));
  const done = ts.filter((t) => t.status === 'completed' && !t.voided && t.graded);
  const judged = done.filter((t) => typeof t.tone_pass === 'boolean');
  const cellKeys = [...new Set(done.map((t) => t.ticket))];
  const allPassCells = cellKeys.filter((tk) => done.filter((t) => t.ticket === tk).every((t) => t.both_ok)).length;
  return {
    trials_run: ts.length,
    completed: done.length,
    voided: ts.filter((t) => t.voided).length,
    harness_errors: ts.filter((t) => t.status === 'harness_error').length,
    rate_limited: ts.filter((t) => t.status === 'rate_limited').length,
    category_acc: mean(done.map((t) => (t.category_ok ? 1 : 0))),
    priority_acc: mean(done.map((t) => (t.priority_ok ? 1 : 0))),
    both_acc: mean(done.map((t) => (t.both_ok ? 1 : 0))),
    cell_all_pass_rate: cellKeys.length ? allPassCells / cellKeys.length : null,
    tone_judged: judged.length,
    tone_pass_rate: mean(judged.map((t) => (t.tone_pass ? 1 : 0))),
    tone_score_mean: mean(judged.map((t) => t.tone_score)),
    runtime_s_mean: mean(done.map((t) => t.runtime_s ?? 0)),
    tool_calls_mean: mean(done.map((t) => t.tool_calls ?? 0)),
    tool_errors_mean: mean(done.map((t) => t.tool_errors ?? 0)),
    tokens_mean: mean(done.map((t) => (t.input_tokens ?? 0) + (t.output_tokens ?? 0))),
    triage_cost_usd: ts.reduce((s, t) => s + (t.cost_usd ?? 0), 0),
  };
}
const metrics = {};
const topupMetrics = {};
for (const c of CONFIGS) {
  metrics[c] = summarize(c, true);
  topupMetrics[c] = summarize(c, false);
}

// ---------- Synthesis ----------
phase('Synthesis');
const failing = [...trials.values()]
  .filter((t) => t.status === 'completed' && !t.voided && (t.both_ok === false || t.tone_pass === false))
  .map((t) => ({
    key: tkey(t), category: t.category, priority: t.priority,
    category_ok: t.category_ok, priority_ok: t.priority_ok,
    tone_pass: t.tone_pass, tone_reason: t.tone_reason, out_path: t.out_path,
  }));

const [failures, critic] = await parallel([
  () => run(`You do failure analysis for round ${ROUND} of the triage agent eval. The trials are finished, so you may read spe/evals/tasks/answers.json, spe/evals/graders/, and the out files under ${RUN_DIR}.
Group the failing trials below into failure types. Give each type a short name, a kind, what happens, how to spot it, the trial keys it was seen in, and a suggested fix. If a failure looks like a wrong reference label or a grader bug rather than an agent error, list it under suspected_grader_bugs with the evidence. Then list what round ${ROUND + 1} should change.

Per-config metrics:
${JSON.stringify(metrics, null, 2)}

Failing trials:
${JSON.stringify(failing, null, 2)}`, { label: 'failure analysis', phase: 'Synthesis', schema: FAILURE_SCHEMA }),

  () => run(`You are the completeness critic for round ${ROUND} of the triage agent eval. Read spe/predictions/r${RR}.yaml. List every predicted metric and config. For each one, say whether the metrics below give a measured number. Then check these points and list every gap you find. Every one of the ${cells.length} cells should have ${TRIALS} completed and graded trials. Every completed trial should have a tone score. Count the trials skipped for the spend cap, the harness errors, and the voided trials. Say whether any config is at the metric's maximum, which would make its prediction not scorable.

Metrics (planned trials only):
${JSON.stringify(metrics, null, 2)}
Skips: ${JSON.stringify(skips)}
Void check: ${JSON.stringify(voidCheck())}
Spent: $${spent.toFixed(2)} of $${BUDGET_USD}. Agents used: ${agentsUsed} of ${MAX_AGENTS}.`, { label: 'completeness critic', phase: 'Synthesis', schema: CRITIC_SCHEMA }),
]);

log(`Done. Spent $${spent.toFixed(2)} of $${BUDGET_USD}. ${skips.length} skips. Critic says complete: ${critic.complete}`);

return {
  round: ROUND,
  dry_run: DRY,
  run_dir: RUN_DIR,
  halted: false,
  budget_overrun: overrun,
  spent_usd: spent,
  agents_used: agentsUsed,
  metrics,
  topup_metrics: topupMetrics,
  split_cells: splitCells.map((c) => c.key),
  skips,
  void: voidCheck(),
  failures,
  critic,
  judge_note: 'The tone judge is Opus, which is the same model family as the agent. No judge from another family was available.',
};
```
